  "kind": "build",
  "title": "# Build: plugin-commands-auto (Urgent profile) Requested by Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice).",
  "asked": "# Build: plugin-commands-auto (Urgent profile) Requested by Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice). GO given. Build it now. ## Rule (already added to _claude/rules/RULES.md on the hub) Every plugin, existing and new, automatically exposes all of its commands and reads through control@1, so they appear in the REST API, the MCP server and the CLI with no extra per-plugin work. Brett drives the console by talking to Claude through axHub, so anything a plugin can do must be reachable that way. ## Base / coordination - Base = claude/token-control-opus (PR #250, contains #246): control@1 contract, REST, MCP, CLI. Also read claude/console-commands (PR #249, console MCP tools / `axf-console` service) and reuse whatever it already does for plugin commands; merge its approach in rather than building a second registry. Say in the PR it merges after #250 and #249. - theme-veto-pass is running on the same base (adds control@1 `pass`); don't conflict with it. - Register in the Urgent profile via orchestrator CLI (id `plugin-commands-auto`, branch claude/plugin-commands-auto) + banner entry. Never hand-edit store.json. ## Steps - s1 Command declaration: plugins declare commands once (plugin.json `commands` and/or the existing action/command bus registrations): id, title, description, input schema, output shape, readOnly/destructive flags, confirm-required. Reuse the framework action vocabulary so existing actions become commands without rewriting. - s2 Auto surfaces: the framework generates, from the registry, REST routes (`/api/control/<plugin>/<command>`), MCP tools (`<plugin>_<command>`, annotations readOnly/destructive), and CLI subcommands (`axf <plugin> <command> --args`), plus help text, all via control@1. Hot-registered when a plugin installs, removed on uninstall. - s3 Reads: every plugin's data gets list/get reads (readOnly) so Claude can read everything, not just issue commands. - s4 Backfill: every existing plugin in apps/console-web/plugins (and the other apps' plugins) gets its commands + reads declared. Inventory them in the report. - s5 Enforcement: plugin lifecycle check + the plugin template/_template fail if a plugin has actions not exposed, or no reads; new-plugin scaffold includes the commands block. - s6 Docs (interactive docs page lists every plugin's commands), help packs, tests, check-theme/check-controls, lifecycle, report `_claude/builds/reports/plugin-commands-auto.md`, THREADS.md, PR. Mark each step done through the store. Code, comments and commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once.",
